00:36:50.280 --> 00:36:50.900
Do you love her?

1036
00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:52.900
I remember they could not get through that scene.

1037
00:36:53.060 --> 00:36:55.720
The two of them were cracking each other up.

1038
00:36:55.840 --> 00:36:57.100
It went on forever.

1039
00:36:57.600 --> 00:36:59.720
Not only do I love that Dwight is like, do you love her?

1040
00:36:59.820 --> 00:37:01.620
I love that Michael's like, I don't know.

1041
00:37:01.740 --> 00:37:02.020
Maybe.

1042
00:37:02.300 --> 00:37:02.920
I can't say.

1043
00:37:02.980 --> 00:37:03.480
I can't say.

1044
00:37:03.600 --> 00:37:04.460
I don't know yet.

1045
00:37:04.620 --> 00:37:05.420
Oh, I don't know.

1046
00:37:05.520 --> 00:37:07.560
The two of them are ridiculous.

1047
00:37:08.140 --> 00:37:12.820
And then you have Roy who decides he's going to try to make up with Pam and he decides to

1048
00:37:12.820 --> 00:37:16.060
start tickling you while you're sitting on Jim's desk.

1049
00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:16.920
It's so awkward.

1050
00:37:17.120 --> 00:37:17.820
Next to Jim.

1051
00:37:17.820 --> 00:37:19.140
I remember filming that scene.

1052
00:37:19.280 --> 00:37:22.220
When I watched it, I felt so uncomfortable for Jim.

1053
00:37:22.420 --> 00:37:23.540
I was like, oh, God, Jim.

1054
00:37:23.780 --> 00:37:25.100
And then he gets up and he walks away.

1055
00:37:25.340 --> 00:37:25.460
Yes.

1056
00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:25.900
Yes.

1057
00:37:26.140 --> 00:37:27.940
So here's something interesting about that.

1058
00:37:28.560 --> 00:37:31.540
I, as Jenna, hate being tickled.

1059
00:37:31.620 --> 00:37:32.260
Yeah, you hate it.

1060
00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:33.240
I don't like it.

1061
00:37:33.320 --> 00:37:33.920
It is not.

1062
00:37:34.080 --> 00:37:36.420
It certainly would not be the way to make up with me.

1063
00:37:36.560 --> 00:37:37.440
You'd make you angry.

1064
00:37:37.560 --> 00:37:37.900
It would.

1065
00:37:38.240 --> 00:37:38.480
Yeah.

1066
00:37:38.540 --> 00:37:39.780
I would be like, no.

1067
00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:45.160
And I think that when I was filming that, I had to really wrap my head around the fact

1068
00:37:45.160 --> 00:37:47.940
this is a way that Jenna and Pam are different.

1069
00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:48.420
Yeah.

1070
00:37:49.360 --> 00:37:51.240
Pam is won over by it.

1071
00:37:51.500 --> 00:37:52.760
Pam is like, oh, come on.

1072
00:37:52.860 --> 00:37:53.220
Oh, no.

1073
00:37:53.440 --> 00:37:54.820
That is how they make up.

1074
00:37:54.980 --> 00:37:55.060
Yeah.

1075
00:37:55.420 --> 00:37:59.760
Pam and Roy are friends again, or I guess engaged again after that moment.

1076
00:38:00.020 --> 00:38:00.660
Whatever they are, they're back.

1077
00:38:00.660 --> 00:38:01.540
Whatever they are, they're back.

1078
00:38:01.540 --> 00:38:09.060
But for me, as Jenna, I had to really stuff all of my Jenna instincts because I do not

1079
00:38:09.060 --> 00:38:09.640
like tickling.

1080
00:38:09.860 --> 00:38:11.660
Well, and some people really don't like being tickled.

1081
00:38:11.820 --> 00:38:13.020
I don't like being scared.

1082
00:38:13.260 --> 00:38:14.440
Oh, I know.

1083
00:38:14.660 --> 00:38:18.020
Well, and my husband, like once a year around Halloween.

1084
00:38:18.140 --> 00:38:21.080
You don't like being startled or scared.

1085
00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:22.620
I don't like scary movies.

1086
00:38:23.080 --> 00:38:23.480
You don't respond well.

1087
00:38:23.620 --> 00:38:24.780
I don't go to scary movies.

1088
00:38:24.900 --> 00:38:26.660
And my dad was the same way.

1089
00:38:26.780 --> 00:38:29.320
So you know how they say some people are like fight or flight?

1090
00:38:29.520 --> 00:38:29.700
Yeah.

1091
00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:30.820
I am fight.

1092
00:38:30.820 --> 00:38:36.040
And so Josh, my husband, like around Halloween, him and the kids think it's funny to get like

1093
00:38:36.040 --> 00:38:38.420
a fake arm or a mask and scare me.

1094
00:38:38.700 --> 00:38:41.940
And I always say to them, one of you will get whacked.

1095
00:38:42.220 --> 00:38:42.820
You know that.

1096
00:38:42.900 --> 00:38:43.440
And I have no control.

1097
00:38:43.440 --> 00:38:45.520
You flail your arms when people scare you.

1098
00:38:45.540 --> 00:38:45.680
Yeah.

1099
00:38:45.680 --> 00:38:46.340
I've seen it happen.

1100
00:38:46.340 --> 00:38:47.760
I have no control over it.

1101
00:38:47.840 --> 00:38:50.620
Just recently, my husband, for Halloween, they jumped out to scare me.

1102
00:38:50.740 --> 00:38:51.520
He had this mask on.

1103
00:38:51.820 --> 00:38:52.980
And I screamed.

1104
00:38:53.160 --> 00:38:55.600
And then with everything I had, I hucked my phone at him.

1105
00:38:55.720 --> 00:38:57.260
And I hit him with my phone.

1106
00:38:58.260 --> 00:38:59.820
Clearly, like I didn't mean to.

1107
00:38:59.820 --> 00:39:02.760
It's just this weird instinctual thing where I just go, whack.

1108
00:39:03.100 --> 00:39:03.320
Yeah.

1109
00:39:03.540 --> 00:39:08.080
You need to hope that you never have to do a scene where someone scares you.

1110
00:39:08.200 --> 00:39:08.800
It'll be very.

1111
00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:09.460
Because you will.

1112
00:39:09.640 --> 00:39:12.420
How will you keep your arms from not whacking?

1113
00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:13.300
I don't know.

1114
00:39:13.580 --> 00:39:14.160
I don't know.

1115
00:39:14.320 --> 00:39:15.920
Someone will get hurt.

1116
00:39:15.920 --> 00:39:20.540
That was the difficulty for me in that scene because tickling me makes me irritated.

1117
00:39:20.820 --> 00:39:21.600
Want to whack someone.

1118
00:39:21.820 --> 00:39:23.200
Does not make me laugh.

1119
00:39:23.940 --> 00:39:25.500
Well, I thought you did a great job.

1120
00:39:25.520 --> 00:39:27.180
And it was cringy as heck.

1121
00:39:27.320 --> 00:39:27.520
Yeah.

1122
00:39:27.660 --> 00:39:27.840
Poor Jim.

1123
00:39:28.060 --> 00:39:28.460
I know.

1124
00:39:28.620 --> 00:39:28.880
All right.

1125
00:39:28.960 --> 00:39:29.700
We're going to go to a break.

1126
00:39:29.820 --> 00:39:30.480
Let's take a break.

1127
00:39:35.580 --> 00:39:38.620
Angela, I want to start by asking you a question.

1128
00:39:39.000 --> 00:39:39.200
Okay.

1129
00:39:39.540 --> 00:39:43.140
You know the scene where Dwight is asking Katie on the date?

1130
00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:43.480
Mm-hmm.

1131
00:39:43.480 --> 00:39:46.300
And it's in front of your character because you're looking at purses.

1132
00:39:46.460 --> 00:39:46.680
Mm-hmm.

1133
00:39:47.080 --> 00:39:51.560
Your face during that moment, what were you thinking?

1134
00:39:52.040 --> 00:39:53.520
I did not even look up.

1135
00:39:53.700 --> 00:39:54.000
No.

1136
00:39:54.160 --> 00:39:55.420
You just kept your eyes down.

1137
00:39:55.540 --> 00:39:56.500
I kept my eyes down.

1138
00:39:56.500 --> 00:39:59.100
And then I didn't look up until he walked out of the room.

1139
00:39:59.140 --> 00:40:02.760
And you can see when he exits, I kind of look up and look at him leave.

1140
00:40:03.040 --> 00:40:06.280
You know, in that moment, it was so awkward and uncomfortable.

1141
00:40:06.480 --> 00:40:08.400
I wasn't given direction to do that.

1142
00:40:08.400 --> 00:40:09.580
But I just felt so uncomfortable.

1143
00:40:09.580 --> 00:40:11.020
I just kept looking down.

1144
00:40:11.220 --> 00:40:13.320
But Dwight is not a thing yet.

1145
00:40:13.480 --> 00:40:13.760
No.

1146
00:40:13.940 --> 00:40:18.700
But it is so easy to superimpose what we know is going to happen between your two characters

1147
00:40:18.700 --> 00:40:20.000
onto this moment.

1148
00:40:20.040 --> 00:40:25.380
But people were asking if you knew that your characters were going to end up together in

1149
00:40:25.380 --> 00:40:26.060
that moment yet.

1150
00:40:26.060 --> 00:40:27.120
But you didn't, right?

1151
00:40:27.340 --> 00:40:27.860
I didn't know.

1152
00:40:27.980 --> 00:40:28.520
I didn't know.

1153
00:40:28.640 --> 00:40:31.740
And just in that conference room, it's not a huge space.

1154
00:40:31.940 --> 00:40:37.340
And him putting himself out there like that to her, I, as Angela, and even as myself,

1155
00:40:37.480 --> 00:40:42.440
felt so uncomfortable that I just was trying somehow not to participate in the moment in

1156
00:40:42.440 --> 00:40:42.920
any way.

1157
00:40:43.080 --> 00:40:44.120
Like try to just be invisible?

1158
00:40:44.360 --> 00:40:44.440
Yeah.

1159
00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:46.540
I was, in my mind, I was like, just be invisible.

1160
00:40:46.920 --> 00:40:50.520
I think that, you know, Angela didn't know that Dwight was going to be her soulmate.

1161
00:40:50.640 --> 00:40:52.700
But I think she did see him as an equal.

1162
00:40:52.720 --> 00:40:54.600
And she respected his work ethic.

1163
00:40:54.800 --> 00:40:58.300
And probably respected who he was in the office, even though he annoyed her.

1164
00:40:58.620 --> 00:40:58.740
Right?

1165
00:40:58.920 --> 00:40:59.160
Sure.

1166
00:40:59.340 --> 00:41:01.240
There was a power struggle between the two of them.

1167
00:41:01.240 --> 00:41:07.200
So to see him sort of humble himself like that to Katie and get humiliated, I just felt

1168
00:41:07.200 --> 00:41:09.980
like I didn't even want him to think that I had witnessed it.

1169
00:41:10.200 --> 00:41:11.260
I didn't see it.

1170
00:41:11.360 --> 00:41:12.060
It didn't happen.

1171
00:41:12.220 --> 00:41:12.620
It's okay.

1172
00:41:12.920 --> 00:41:14.760
That's, I think, what she was thinking.

1173
00:41:14.880 --> 00:41:16.400
And that's why I didn't look up.

1174
00:41:16.500 --> 00:41:18.620
I was literally trying to be invisible in the moment.

1175
00:41:18.900 --> 00:41:23.880
Well, after that, you have a line that is one of my favorite lines of your character

1176
00:41:23.880 --> 00:41:25.700
where you describe your favorite colors.

1177
00:41:26.400 --> 00:41:28.080
This is a fan question from Emmy.

1178
00:41:28.260 --> 00:41:32.100
Angela, did you improvise the scene where you discuss your colors being different shades

1179
00:41:32.100 --> 00:41:32.540
of gray?

1180
00:41:32.780 --> 00:41:33.520
Yes, I did.

1181
00:41:33.660 --> 00:41:34.500
I knew it.

1182
00:41:34.660 --> 00:41:35.200
Yes, I did.

1183
00:41:35.360 --> 00:41:40.880
In the episode, Dwight is looking in at the conference room at Katie and Angela sort of

1184
00:41:40.880 --> 00:41:41.280
talking.

1185
00:41:41.440 --> 00:41:43.160
And we didn't have any scripted dialogue.

1186
00:41:43.160 --> 00:41:44.940
So they said, can you just kind of banter?

1187
00:41:45.140 --> 00:41:47.840
And I didn't even know if it would make it in, you know?

1188
00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:50.200
And so that scene was improvised.

1189
00:41:50.380 --> 00:41:54.500
And it starts off with Amy as Katie saying, well, you seem to like to touch things.

1190
00:41:54.980 --> 00:41:59.040
And then I just responded, I don't like to necessarily touch things.

1191
00:41:59.040 --> 00:42:00.300
I'm shopping, you know?

1192
00:42:00.460 --> 00:42:01.260
I loved that line.

1193
00:42:01.420 --> 00:42:03.100
And then she said, well, what color do you like?

1194
00:42:03.160 --> 00:42:04.140
And this was all improvised.

1195
00:42:04.260 --> 00:42:07.120
And I said, gray, dark gray, charcoal.

1196
00:42:07.920 --> 00:42:09.460
And it made it in.

1197
00:42:09.540 --> 00:42:10.500
And that was really fun.

1198
00:42:10.660 --> 00:42:13.700
And then that line ended up in a article in the newspaper.

1199
00:42:13.700 --> 00:42:16.360
It was talking about what sums up the show.

1200
00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:21.820
And they said, well, the character Angela's line, gray, dark gray, charcoal, really sets

1201
00:42:21.820 --> 00:42:22.380
the tone.

1202
00:42:22.380 --> 00:42:24.180
And I was so proud of that.

1203
00:42:24.500 --> 00:42:28.400
It really then informed a lot of your wardrobe after that.

1204
00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:33.480
You had been kind of wearing these muted colors, but that became your uniform moving forward.

1205
00:42:33.780 --> 00:42:35.180
Okay, Jenna, what else do you have?

1206
00:42:35.320 --> 00:42:35.660
All right.

1207
00:42:35.880 --> 00:42:41.120
The scene where Ryan and Michael are cleaning out his car, that was not improvised.

1208
00:42:41.300 --> 00:42:42.200
No, that was scripted.

1209
00:42:42.280 --> 00:42:48.580
A lot of people asked, all of it, blue blast, smell alike, how many filet of fish do you eat?

1210
00:42:48.700 --> 00:42:50.100
All of those lines are in the script.

1211
00:42:50.100 --> 00:42:55.320
I checked because when I was watching it, it was so hard for me to believe that it was not

1212
00:42:55.320 --> 00:42:58.020
improvised that I went back to my script and I read it.

1213
00:42:58.140 --> 00:43:03.000
And I think that it just points to how good the writing was on our show.

1214
00:43:03.320 --> 00:43:03.500
Fantastic.

1215
00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:04.820
Just how good.

1216
00:43:04.960 --> 00:43:07.440
And also how good the actors were.

1217
00:43:08.040 --> 00:43:13.640
I mean, BJ and Steve in that scene, just absolutely brilliant.

1218
00:43:14.060 --> 00:43:19.720
Mindy also told me that the reference to the filet of fishes is a nod to her disgusting love

1219
00:43:19.720 --> 00:43:20.960
of filet of fish in real life.

1220
00:43:20.960 --> 00:43:22.780
Or just her love for McDonald's.

1221
00:43:22.900 --> 00:43:24.560
She loves McDonald's.

1222
00:43:25.900 --> 00:43:28.320
But that she really does love a filet of fish.

1223
00:43:28.480 --> 00:43:34.600
I loved in this scene, too, when Michael's like, that was over a period of time, okay?

1224
00:43:34.600 --> 00:43:35.400
It was over a month.

1225
00:43:35.480 --> 00:43:36.160
It was over a month.

1226
00:43:36.540 --> 00:43:38.320
And Ryan the Temp goes, still.

1227
00:43:38.640 --> 00:43:38.920
Yeah.

1228
00:43:40.040 --> 00:43:42.060
I could watch that scene over and over again.

1229
00:43:42.200 --> 00:43:43.060
I think that's a gem.

1230
00:43:43.380 --> 00:43:47.480
I think if you haven't rewatched this episode, but you're listening to the podcast, just please

1231
00:43:47.480 --> 00:43:48.480
go watch that scene.

1232
00:43:48.620 --> 00:43:49.220
It's so good.

1233
00:43:49.820 --> 00:43:50.780
Blue is not a flavor.

1234
00:43:51.820 --> 00:43:52.900
I have a note card.

1235
00:43:53.120 --> 00:43:53.700
Say it.

1236
00:43:54.020 --> 00:43:54.240
Okay.

1237
00:43:54.400 --> 00:43:57.260
This is a great, great Dwight line when he says,

1238
00:43:57.600 --> 00:43:59.500
shroots produce very thirsty babies.

1239
00:43:59.800 --> 00:44:00.620
Oh, yes.

1240
00:44:00.820 --> 00:44:01.880
That's a famous line.

1241
00:44:02.000 --> 00:44:02.860
That's a famous line.

1242
00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:06.120
And when I was pregnant, I was pregnant season five of The Office.

1243
00:44:06.320 --> 00:44:11.720
And I got a gift of a t-shirt that said, shroots produce very thirsty babies.

1244
00:44:11.720 --> 00:44:13.180
And it was a maternity shirt.

1245
00:44:13.340 --> 00:44:14.140
Oh, my gosh.

1246
00:44:14.240 --> 00:44:18.280
And I wore that around my big belly and people would freak out.

1247
00:44:18.300 --> 00:44:19.340
I still have it.

1248
00:44:19.420 --> 00:44:20.120
I still have it.

1249
00:44:20.200 --> 00:44:20.640
Oh.

1250
00:44:20.640 --> 00:44:22.340
Do you have a picture of yourself in that?

1251
00:44:22.660 --> 00:44:23.340
I will look.

1252
00:44:23.400 --> 00:44:25.940
But if I don't, I'll just take a picture of myself in it.

1253
00:44:26.040 --> 00:44:29.240
And I'll have to post that on Office Ladies Pod because I still have that shirt.

1254
00:44:29.440 --> 00:44:29.840
You should.

1255
00:44:29.980 --> 00:44:30.220
Definitely.

1256
00:44:30.760 --> 00:44:33.200
Here is something that everybody wrote in about.

1257
00:44:33.320 --> 00:44:35.060
This was one of our most popular questions.

1258
00:44:35.840 --> 00:44:39.340
What's up with the wrong parking lot at the end of this episode?

1259
00:44:39.560 --> 00:44:43.240
That's because this was the original set before we moved.

1260
00:44:43.240 --> 00:44:47.560
The first six episodes, we all filmed at an actual office building in Culver City.

1261
00:44:47.620 --> 00:44:48.780
And that was the parking lot.

1262
00:44:48.780 --> 00:44:49.260
Yes.

1263
00:44:49.520 --> 00:44:53.380
So when we moved in season two and beyond, we had two soundstages.

1264
00:44:53.560 --> 00:44:59.980
One soundstage was a recreation of the office, that interior office that we shot in the first year.

1265
00:44:59.980 --> 00:45:02.940
The other building is where the writers worked.

1266
00:45:03.040 --> 00:45:04.300
And it was just an office building.

1267
00:45:04.300 --> 00:45:06.360
And that was just the parking lot for it.

1268
00:45:06.560 --> 00:45:06.880
Yes.

1269
00:45:07.040 --> 00:45:10.400
And that is where we filmed the Dunder Mifflin parking lot.

1270
00:45:10.400 --> 00:45:15.660
So it was really interesting because we had our warehouse set over there.

1271
00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:17.780
And then we had the parking lot.

1272
00:45:17.960 --> 00:45:20.500
And we had the lobby and the elevator where Hank's at.

1273
00:45:20.680 --> 00:45:21.020
Yes.

1274
00:45:21.160 --> 00:45:22.460
All of that was one building.

1275
00:45:22.460 --> 00:45:24.780
But then the Dunder Mifflin building was something else.

1276
00:45:24.820 --> 00:45:28.840
So if we had to do a scene where you see us walk out,

1277
00:45:28.860 --> 00:45:36.680
we would have to start that scene in one building and then move all the cameras and all of us over to the other building and then get the exterior version of it.

1278
00:45:36.820 --> 00:45:37.220
Yes.

1279
00:45:37.320 --> 00:45:38.200
It was quite complicated.

1280
00:45:38.200 --> 00:45:44.900
It was basically when we filmed in one stage indoors, we filmed another stage outdoors for the most part.

1281
00:45:45.060 --> 00:45:51.180
But that parking lot is not the Dunder Mifflin parking lot that you see from season two and beyond.

1282
00:45:51.440 --> 00:45:53.400
And I have a story about that parking lot.

1283
00:45:53.580 --> 00:45:59.900
You see in that final shot, it starts with Michael and Jim and Katie leaving.

1284
00:46:00.320 --> 00:46:01.400
She's got her big bag.

1285
00:46:01.560 --> 00:46:05.660
Michael realizes that Jim is going to be giving her a ride home because they're going to get drinks.

1286
00:46:05.660 --> 00:46:13.640
And then it reveals Pam and Roy backing up in Roy's truck and Pam clocks Jim and Katie.

1287
00:46:14.660 --> 00:46:23.040
So David and I had to sit in that truck in the parking lot and wait a very long time until everyone came out and did that scene.

1288
00:46:23.040 --> 00:46:26.260
And we had a little walkie talkie inside the truck and they would say, go.

